    "body": "## Scope\nAdd one reviewable design proposal for a private Chat03 match between exactly the owner and one trusted invitee.\n\n- Defines owner-mediated invitation, individualized bearer handoff, two-device join/reconnect, device-loss and ambiguous replace recovery.\n- Compares the practical bearer pilot with passkey-bound identity and states the stolen-token limitation plainly.\n- Maps proposal steps to current Worker APIs, capability generation/revoke/replace, commit/reveal, admin boundary, and PA-01..09.\n- Includes the two-device fault/abuse test matrix and the next narrow implementation atom.\n\n## Baseline and boundaries\n- Branch created from live `main@31b7a077820914e92de81239e5ab4099e3dfa558` (PR #448 merged).\n- PR #449 HEAD `de6a6130622097d7123b3f4d6ce2da18bea1d9d3` remains open/Ready for review and unmerged; its owner-reported Safari PASS covers only the local synthetic harness.\n- Exactly one documentation file added: `gameplay-server/PRIVATE_ALPHA_TWO_PERSON_ACCESS_SPEC.md`.\n- No Worker, SQL, UI, CSP, token, telemetry, Stage 7.15, Chat04/05, Cloudflare resource, or main changes.\n- No deployment, staging setup, real-person invitation, retention period, operator assignment, or PA decision is approved by this proposal.\n\n## Review request\nPlease review the proposed bearer-risk decision and API/lifecycle mapping. Keep this Draft until the owner accepts or amends the decisions. No merge or runtime acceptance is claimed.",
